  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a finite scalar construction on the selected PR1263 word. A joint exact dynamic program for L253/L254 offsets in `[-4,4]^2` lowers the complete scalar invoice by **364 complex primitives per invocation in both orientations**:\n\n| Orientation | Baseline | Joint schedule | Saving |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Forward | 136,002 | 135,638 | 364 |\n| Backward | 136,018 | 135,654 | 364 |\n\nThe 96 and 120 incident-ADD supports share one event (19427). The bounded joint optimum equals the invoice from the separately optimized schedules; both offsets are zero at the shared event. This package makes no new \u03ba claim and does not change the selected record.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- Base: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`.\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- PR1263 source: `5fbaca13028846bddbb001e8e07addc2ab8e5816`; PR1350 L253 schedule: `64b8a55c6933ffb6d9e30fa19f85d05b572d4aa5`.\n- The DP covers 215 union ADDs with 81 offset-pair states and charges all coefficient changes, 45 inserted SCALE macros, and 52 real-component scale work.\n- Both emitted words pass all 712 formal columns. The 192-bit charge and recursive paid profile are unchanged. The one shared-ADD coefficient mutation and one omitted-transition-scale mutation reject in each orientation.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-l253-l254-joint-temporal-seedde1\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/complex-l253-l254-joint-temporal-seedde1 outcome=completed`.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThis proves the minimum only inside the stated `[-4,4]^2` exponent box. It does not certify a global all-integer optimum, native or hosted admission, a new \u03ba, or the multiplication theorem. See `README.md`, `PROOF.md`, `TASK.json`, `SOURCES.json`, and `VALIDATION.json` for the cost argument, source pins, controls, and limits.\n\nCredit PR1263 and Philipp / @mightyOil for the frozen word; Sagar Thakrar / @thakrarsagar and PR1350 for the L253 schedule; Sagar Thakrar and PR1259 for the temporal-gauge method; and PR1161 for the lowerer lineage. Prepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\nThe required local claim is in the package. The authenticated Discussions API remained rate-limited, so a public CLAIM reply could not be posted; overlap was refreshed through paginated PR REST results and current public Discussions #1163 and #1167.",
